From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: libraries (IShellLibrary, CLSID_ShellLibrary)

CLSID_ShellLibrary was not registered, so programs that look up a library's folders
(foobar2000 asks for the Music library's at every start) got REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG. A library is a set of
folders kept in a .library-ms file under FOLDERID_Libraries (the documented library description schema:
name, owner, pinned flag, icon, folder type and one search connector per folder, with the owner's and
other users' default save locations). The object loads one from a shell item or a known folder (the
standard Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos libraries come from the user's and the public known
folders until a file exists), adds and removes folders, lists them as an IShellItemArray (filtered to
file system or storage items), resolves one, keeps the default save locations, options, folder type
and icon, and commits back to its file or saves a new one (fail if there, override, or a unique name).
Known folder URLs (knownfolder:{id}), file: URLs and paths are read; paths are written.
include: IShellLibrary and its enumerations, the ShellLibrary coclass.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/Makefile.in b/dlls/shell32/Makefile.in
index 7398d69..6bae9c0 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/shell32/Makefile.in
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	fileopdlg.c \
 	folders.c \
 	iconcache.c \
+	library.c \
 	new_menu.c \
 	openwith.c \
 	pidl.c \
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/library.c b/dlls/shell32/library.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a3d19c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/shell32/library.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1065 @@
+/*
+ * Shell libraries (IShellLibrary, CLSID_ShellLibrary)
+ *
+ * Copyright 2026 Stained Glass OS contributors
+ *
